1 | devops | Branch feat/ac-handover-identity from origin/main. Amend the PRD per issue 2340 comment 5653381861. In docs/prd/pages/assistant-channel.md: section 3.2 gains one sentence that a web_url for a trip this channel created lands per section 7.4; add section 7.4, The handover landing, stating the three cases (owner signed in continues with the chosen option selected; owner signed out signs in first, page shell stays mounted behind the modal, then continues without reload; any other signed-in account receives a copy in its own account at a new trip id and continues there; a guest signs in or signs up first) and that the original is never modified or booked by anyone but its owner; section 9 gains S19, the line shown once after a copy, text This trip is now saved in your account., marked PROPOSED, rendered only when ACCEPTED. In docs/prd/pages/06-conversation-results.md: section 4 Direct URL gains a row for a record whose origin is assistant (sign-in required at landing, then own-or-copy); add section 13.3.3, Assistant-originated records, stating the API behaviour: GET by a guest answers 401, GET by a signed-in non-owner answers 403 with error code not_owner, GET by the owner answers 200 interactive, and a non-existent id answers the byte-identical 404; the website share model of 13.3.1 is unchanged for records whose origin is web; section 13.6 clone row moves from proposal to contract per 13.3.3: POST /result-sessions/{id}/clone by a signed-in caller copies intent, parsed_fields, result_snapshot, selected_offer_id and view into a new record owned by the caller, strips the assistant_owner and assistant_revision keys, keeps the origin, answers 201 with the full interactive entity, 401 for a guest, 404 for an unknown id, 409 when the caller already owns the source. Date every amendment 2026-09-13, name the co-founder, cite the comment. VERIFY: make check-prd-index exit 0. HOUSE STYLE: no long dash anywhere, no AI tool or vendor name, no Co-Authored-By trailer. Commit and push. | feat/ac-handover-identity

